Ladybird lets the shadow editor and placeholder grow to fit
the rendered line. Blink computes the editor’s line sizing in
TextControlInnerEditorElement::CustomStyleForLayoutObject. WebKit’s
RenderTextControlSingleLine::layout accounts for both the line
box and its content height. Gecko’s forms.css puts white-space:pre
on the editing root and placeholder and clips placeholder
overflow on the inline axis.

Chrome 158.0.8127.37, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 painted
all 36 rows of the enlarged fallback glyph in the value and
placeholder of a 60px input. Ladybird’s fixed one-line shadow boxes
exposed only 20 of those rows.
